==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 15.4 Update|Version 15.4]], Mythic Cats were called Legend Cats in the [[Legend Stages/OPED (Old)|Stories of Legend opening and ending]] and [[Catclaw Championships]] [[Catnip Challenges]].
**This change was likely made to prevent confusion with [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cats]].
**In [[BCJP]], Mythic Cats and Legend Rare Cats use different words for "legend": Mythic Cats are レジェンド ''Rejendo Nyanko'' (Legend Cats), whereas Legend Rare Cats are 伝説レア ''Densetsu Rea'' (Legend Rare).
*In the [[Enigma Stages]] tutorial, Mythic Cats are called "legendary Cats" ("Legend Cats" pre-15.4).
*[[Lowkey]]'s Japanese description states that a fight to the death against Mythic Cats (still referred to as "Legend Cats" in [[BCJP]]) resulted in his extinction in modern times.
*[[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]], [[Masked Yulala (Special Cat)|Masked Yulala]], [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs & Fenrir]] and [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]] have many similarities:
**Counting Yulala's Japanese name (Urara), their names all start with "Ur".
**Their Japanese descriptions all start with a quote followed by how they joined the Cat Army, which always includes the word 勝手 (''katte'', meaning "selfish", "self-serving" or "acting on one's own without asking").
**Their attack animations all include electricity.
**All have anti-[[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] abilities and Immunity to Curse in at least one of their forms.
*Among the masked Mythic Cats (Ururun Wolf, [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Masked Grandmaster Cat]], Masked Yulala, Master Uril, Urs & Fenrir, [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Elder Mask Doron]] and [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]]), Ururun is the only one without a Relic enemy counterpart (counting her separately from Urs).
*From [[Version 3.5 Update|Version 3.5]] to [[Version 5.0 Update|5.0]], there was unused text meant for a preview of a [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]] dropped from the final [[Stories of Legend]] stage, formatted as: "Stories of Legend Clear Reward|Clear the Stories of Legend for a|chance to get the Super Rare unit |●●●●●●●!"
**Note that at the time, Ururun Wolf and [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]] were the only drop units from Stories of Legend. Ultimately, [[Mecha-Bun (Special Cat)|Mecha-Bun]] does not have its own preview, is a Mythic Cat rather than Super Rare, and is a guaranteed reward, not chance-based.
*All Mythic Cats unlocked from Stories of Legend, Uncanny Legends, or the Heavenly Tower stages are either always Immune to Curse or eventually gain this ability. They also either always have anti-relic abilities or eventually gain them.
*[[Moneko (Special Cat)|Moneko]] and [[Bean Cats (Special Cat)|Bean Cats]] are the only non-Mythic Cats unlocked from the Main Chapters.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] has an unused idle animation that is only seen in the [[Into the Future]] Chapter 3 preview.
*Unlike other Mythic Cats, [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Elder Beast Naala]]'s preview displayed when entering Legend Stages shows its [[Ultima Beast Naala|enemy counterpart]]: one can tell from the shape of its tail and the idol on its back.
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], most Mythic Cats had a 3% drop rate from their respective stages. 15.3 increased the drop rate to 30%.

